              The  _b_u_f  and _s_i_z_e arguments are, respectively, a buffer of data
              to be output to the stream and the size of that buffer.  As  its
              function  result, the _w_r_i_t_e function should return the number of
              bytes copied from _b_u_f, or 0 on error.  (The  function  must  not
