              SSEEEEKK__EENNDD
                     The stream offset should be set to the size of the stream
                     plus _*_o_f_f_s_e_t.

              Before returning, the _s_e_e_k function should update _*_o_f_f_s_e_t to in‐
              dicate the new stream offset.

              As its function result, the _s_e_e_k function  should  return  0  on
              success, and -1 on error.

              If  _*_s_e_e_k  is a null pointer, then it is not possible to perform
              seek operations on the stream.

